IO::Async::Process spec in _execute_command pipes stdout only; the result always returns stderr => "". Callers and _format_result therefore never see stderr, and the compress path receives an empty stderr. Add a stderr pipe_read handler and thread it through, or document the omission as intended.

2026-09-09 11:12 Left open as a maintainer design decision, not done autonomously. The ticket (high priority) says capture stderr, but the house rules and the documented architecture state stdout-only capture is the intended model and call the stderr omission a known scope gap, not a bug to silently fix; the ticket itself offers the alternative to document the omission as intended. Capturing stderr changes the run tool output contract (a behavior/API change). Question for the maintainer: (a) add stderr capture and thread it through result, _format_result and compress, or (b) document the omission as intended? Also unverifiable until ticket 5 (baseline red).

